# Build context for playground/api/Dockerfile ONLY.
#
# BuildKit prefers `<dockerfile>.dockerignore` over the root `.dockerignore`, which is why this
# file is scoped here: the root file also governs the OpenEnv env-server images, and an allowlist
# tuned for the playground would silently starve those builds.
#
# WHY AN ALLOWLIST. The root `.dockerignore` is a denylist, and it missed enough that the context
# for this image measured 4.017 GiB -- model weights under eval/, datasets under data/, notebooks
# under training/, sibling package trees, and two staged HF Space checkouts. None of it is copied
# by the Dockerfile; all of it was uploaded. A denylist fails open, so every new heavy directory
# joins the context by default. Starting from `*` fails closed: a new directory is excluded until
# someone names it, which is the correct default for something that is uploaded on every build.

*

# --- Python package installed into the image ---
!pyproject.toml
!README.md
!dataforge/
!constitutions/

# --- Playground API ---
!playground/api/requirements.txt
!playground/api/app.py
!playground/api/samples/
!playground/api/slowapi.env

# --- Frontend sources needed by the `web` build stage ---
!playground/web/package.json
!playground/web/package-lock.json
!playground/web/index.html
!playground/web/vite.config.ts
!playground/web/tsconfig.json
!playground/web/tsconfig.app.json
!playground/web/tsconfig.node.json
!playground/web/config.js
!playground/web/src/
!playground/web/public/
!playground/web/scripts/

# --- Re-exclude artefacts that live inside the allowed trees ---
playground/web/node_modules/
playground/web/dist/
playground/web/test-results/
playground/web/playwright-report/
playground/api/web/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/*.pyo
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
